Institutional principle

Scientific authority should be accompanied by methodological transparency, evidentiary traceability, nomenclature accuracy, and accessible communication.

+1HP — Epistemic Articulacy

Evidence establishes credibility. Measurement establishes precision. Methodology establishes reproducibility. Articulacy establishes accessibility.

This architecture is a proposed interdisciplinary classification framework, not an internationally recognized scientific taxonomy. Its strength is providing a consistent indexing structure without confusing internal nomenclature with established scientific standards.
